{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Patchset 2 — the CI `-1`, and what it caught\n\nPatchset 1 took `Verified -1`. Two independent causes, one mine.\n\n### Not mine: definition-vs-tree skew (`optionality / clean core wheel`, 47s)\n\n```\nERROR: file or directory not found: tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_registry_distribution.py\ncollected 0 items  ->  exit 4\n```\n\nThe Gerrit Verified lane takes the workflow DEFINITION from the target branch but checks out\nthe CHANGE'S tree. `origin/main` had gained both that test file and the `_optionality.yml:114`\nline that runs it; my patchset's base predated both. Six changes were reddened by it. Filed as\n`anxious-resistant-urson`, and the guard has since landed in change 2002.\n\nWorth naming: that is **the same bug class as `7e90-233b-3ee9-4f14`** — the origin ticket this\nbug attributes site 1 to. `_build-and-test.yml` documents the if-present guard for exactly this\nskew; the new step did not copy it. The bug I am fixing and the gate that failed my fix for it\nare the same defect, one layer apart.\n\n### Mine: a bare `_child_diag` import that cannot survive a nested pytest run\n\nFour pytest jobs, two tests, one cause:\n\n```\nImportError: Error importing plugin \"tests.interfaces.facades.test_cli\": No module named '_child_diag'\n```\n\n`tests/unit/test_fixture_env_repr_security.py` lists `tests.interfaces.facades.test_cli` in\n`_FIXTURE_SURFACES` and loads it as a `pytest_plugins` entry in a NESTED pytest run whose test\nfile lives in a tmp basetemp OUTSIDE `tests/`. There the root `tests/conftest.py` never loads,\nso the `sys.path` injection every bare `from _child_diag import …` depends on never happens.\n\n**I predicted this and under-weighted it.** The residual-risk note on the previous comment says\nthe bare import \"resolves only because the root `tests/conftest.py` puts `tests/` on\n`sys.path`\", and I had already hit that exact `ModuleNotFoundError` in a scratch probe. I\ndispositioned it \"matched the repo's existing pattern\" without checking whether any consumer\nloads these modules outside that context. One does.\n\nFixed with the explicit `sys.path` bootstrap the `0e1d` precedent\n(`tests/unit/test_live_dc_pass_health.py`) already uses, applied to all five site files.\nImport robustness only — no assertion added, removed, or weakened. Still **0 deletions**.\n\n## The finding that outlasts this ticket\n\nI reported \"full suite green, 11950 passed\" and pushed on it. That log had an mtime **five\nhours older than my change**: a stale file from a previous session. My own sweep never\nfinished, so the second never started, and I read a leftover and called it mine.\n\n> **A log that says \"passed\" is indistinguishable from a log that says \"passed\" about\n> different code.**\n\nThat is the same shape as the bug this ticket is about, and it happened FIVE times in this\nsession's own instruments — a colorized `grep \"^FAILED\"` that reported zero failures\nunconditionally; a truncated sweep log identical to a clean one; an orphaned subshell reported\nas finished; a `pgrep -f \"make test\"` that matched the monitor's own command line and waited on\nitself; and the stale log above. Every one was caught only by checking the instrument against a\nknown-positive case. The first would have shipped a change claiming a clean kill matrix I had\nnever actually measured.\n\n> **If you are verifying an absence, verify your instrument can still see a presence.**\n\nGeneralised as a review criterion in story `sphinxian-agrarian-snake`: ask of any check —\n*can this produce its passing result for any reason other than the condition it claims to\nverify?*\n\n## Verification for patchset 2\n\nFull suite green on the exact committed tree, and this time provably so: a freshly created\nlog that records the sha it started on (matching `HEAD`), an explicit `END` sentinel, and a\ncaptured exit code — `EXITCODE=0`, **15209 passed, 55 skipped, 297 deselected, 1 xfailed**.\nRebased onto current `origin/main`; targeted re-check after the rebase 102 passed / 1 skipped;\n`make lint` clean with the ratchet at `new=0 increased=0 stale=0`; `make typecheck` clean."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787325805940592001,"uuid":"a419b116-43cf-4963-b21b-9c6baec32326"}